      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Will modules need to add a lot of these hidden-API files too BCP fragments?\n\nAny module that contains class members whose signatures are listed in one of the files in frameworks/base/boot/hiddenapi/ will need these files. That is basically legacy code.\n\n\u003e Why are there so many files?\n\nLegacy reasons. The app compat team added files as and when they needed a new one.\n\n\u003e ... it\u0027s not possible to be more opinionated,...\n\nI presume you meant that to be a question not a statement.\n\nWe could but I don\u0027t like that as it looks like magic. This way the relationship is clear. These files are not likely to be touched by module owners at all. There is a presubmit check that (indirectly) prevents any new entries being added to these files. Ideally, module owners will gradually remove these entries as they switch over to using UnsupportedAppUsage. Much longer term these files will be removed when we no longer need to support the older versions of the API.\n\nI have a script that will extract the entries for a specific module and generate the snippet to be inserted here. So, it should be very consistent.",
